WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.470
- It is stunning to me
that the majority of people

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:05.705
that are watching this right
now, have first world problems.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:09.890
(instrumental piano music)

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.370
I see so many young people rightfully so,

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.650
and makes me admire
them, be so altruistic.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.800
Yet they're so weak inside themselves.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.270
They act as though they
want to help the world,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.370
as a way to build confid-, you know,

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.240
it's a facade.
- Ego.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.645
- It's ego.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:25.645 --> 00:00:28.490
- And that's fine and it's a
lot better than other things.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.410
So I don't judge.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.900
It's just, I wasn't able
to give this much back

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.730
until I scratched a
couple things for myself.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.640
- I'm stuck, I'm in rut.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.473
- Because?

00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:41.614
- Because I just finished
army, which is two years,

00:00:41.614 --> 00:00:44.134
so I just came by, I really
don't know what I want to do

00:00:44.134 --> 00:00:45.860
I don't qualify right now.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.023
- You gotta try stuff.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.650
The biggest reason you don't
know what you want to do

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.490
is you haven't tasted enough things

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.470
and the biggest reason you
not tasting enough things,

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.930
is you worried about finding it too fast.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.480
It's Patience.
- Lost in life.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.370
- It's Patience, you can't be lost in life

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.370
when you're this young,

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:02.790
you just have to change your mindset.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.500
Like to me when I look around,

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.240
this many people being in their 20s,

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:10.150
like everybody judging
themselves way too early.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:13.080
What I would do is gather as
many experiences as possible.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.863
Almost everything is perspective.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.440
I think, I think I'm just starting,

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.440
so imagine what I think for most of you.

00:01:22.172 --> 00:01:23.490
- Thank you so much.
- Patience.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.820
Patience, you know whether
it's your parents or yourself

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.570
or people, everybody is trying
to prove something so early.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:34.230
Too many people view post
university as like oh shit

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.150
this is now real and I'm lost,

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.330
they don't put it in the context

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.240
of being alive for a 100 years

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.530
and realizing they are
only 20% of the way done.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.255
Everybody's got strengths and weaknesses,

00:01:44.255 --> 00:01:47.733
what a 60 year old has in
experience but doesn't have time.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.590
So they trade on experience.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.140
What youth has is time,

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.251
you can literally do four different things

00:01:54.251 --> 00:01:56.620
over the next two years,
six months at a time

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:00.030
to figure out, everything
that you think you might like,

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.233
you should try to do.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.160
But that's not what people tell you to do.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.533
- Yeah, they tell you to get a job.

00:02:05.533 --> 00:02:08.820
- Your not lost in life your
just early in the process.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:09.830
You know what I mean?

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.500
You're lost by other peoples standards

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.365
not by your actual, if you
actually took it practically,

00:02:14.365 --> 00:02:15.633
you haven't even started.

00:02:16.621 --> 00:02:20.288
(instrumental piano music)

